Documentation for mmig_AOn1
---------------------------
rev 0.1, 02/10/00:   Initial release
rev 0.2, 06/12/00:   Added VectorInput option


This generator is used to derive AOn1's and AOIn1's.  These gates differ
from those in the standard cell library in that they can be generated
with larger drive sizes, and/or more AND inputs, than the standard cells.


GENERATOR ARGUMENTS:
--------------------
  NAndInputs:
    Definition: 
      The number of AND inputs.
    Legal values:
      2 <= NINPUTS <= 128
    Default:
      4

  OutputAssertion:
    Definition:
      The desired assertion level of the output signal.  The user may
      select H or L.  Inputs are always assumed to be high asserted.
    Legal Values:
      H (high) or L (low)
    Default:
      H

  OutputSize:
    Definition:
      The desired output drive strength.
    Legal Values:
      B, C, D, E
    Default:
      B

  VectorInput:
    Definition:
      The user may choose to compress all of the AND/NAND input pins 
      into a vector, rather than having an individual pin per input.
    Legal Values:
      0 or 1
    Default:
      0

  BitSlice:
    Definition:
      The user may choose to force the gates to be placed within one
      bit pitch (BitSlice = 1) or to allow the gates to be placed
      within one row, in as many bit pitches as necessary (BitSlice = 
      0).  The former is more useful for datapath applications, the
      latter is more useful for control sections.
    Legal Values:
      0 or 1
    Default:
      0

  ReduceInputLoad:
    Definition:
      This parameter causes the default size for the input gates to
      be changed from B to A, if possible.  

      Note that there are some combinations of OutputSize, OutputAssertion,
      and NAndInputS which make reduction of the input gate size impossible.

      Selecting ReduceInputLoad=1 may result in a slower circuit than if
      ReduceInputLoad=0.
    Legal Values:
      0 or 1
    Default:
      0
